 "local_baseline": "qwen3.5:4b-q4_K_M",
 "rule": "* the local model (qwen3.5:4b-q4_K_M) is the default and keeps the task unless a candidate is no worse on every safety figure AND better on the quality figure by the margin of the task;\n  * real-time dialogue (patient, staff): quality at least equal, no more leaks than local, 95th percentile under the 4 s budget; among eligible models the best quality, then the lower median wins;\n  * offline generation (narrative, critic, judge, trap writer): quality better by at least 5 points, false alarms no higher; speed alone never moves an offline task to the cloud;\n  * a task with no benchmark, or whose candidate is not better, stays local.",
 "caveat": "The prompts of the six cloud-selected tasks were written and adjusted while measuring on these same synthetic sets (the 12 approved cases for dialogue, an AI-written staff set, the seeded-defect sets), so the figures are development figures, not held-out evidence; human ratings and fresh sets are DT-250.",
